window.docContents[24].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___15-Graphics/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___15-Graphics--___4___15-Graphics--___4___15_LPAR_ii_RPAR_-Complex-Arguments___-Conformal-Maps":{"contents":"Source: DLMF §4.15(ii).\n\n The map w=sin z sends the strip −π/2 < Re z < π/2 onto the w-plane\ncut along the real axis from −∞ to −1 and from 1 to ∞; z=arcsin w\nis the principal inverse.  Horizontal lines map to confocal ellipses with\nfoci ±1, while vertical lines map to confocal rectangular hyperbolas.  For\nr>0, the four-row source correspondence table has labels\nA,B,C,C̄,D,D̄,E,Ē,F; the C/C̄ and E/Ē entries retain distinct upper\nand lower slit sides, written +i0 and −i0, rather than collapsing them.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.15 Graphics\u0009§4.15 Graphics","header":"§4.15(ii) Complex Arguments: Conformal Maps","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___15-Graphics/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___15-Graphics--___4___15-Graphics--___4___15_LPAR_ii_RPAR_-Complex-Arguments___-Conformal-Maps"},"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___3-Graphics/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___3-Graphics--___6___3-Graphics":{"contents":"This section is graphical rather than a formula list. The real-variable\nfigures show the named exponential, sine, and cosine integrals on finite\nintervals; the complex-variable figure shows the principal E₁ surface,\nincluding its negative-real-axis cut and logarithmic growth near the origin.\nThe linked DLMF graphics and captions remain the primary disclosures; the\nLean vocabulary below records only their concrete plotting ranges and cut.\n\nThe real-variable graphics are identified as having been produced at NIST.\n\nThe real-variable subsection introduces the two graphs and directs readers to\nthe exponential, sine, and cosine integral functions named in their captions.\nFor a graph of the logarithmic integral li(x), the source directs readers\nto Figure 6.16.2.\n\nNIST identifies the real-variable graphics as NIST-produced. Figure 6.3.1\nplots E₁(x) and Ei(x) for 0 < x <= 2.\n\nFigure 6.3.2 plots Si(x) and Ci(x) for 0 <= x <= 15.\n\nThe complex-variable surface is identified as having been produced at NIST.\n\nThe complex-variable subsection records a NIST-produced surface and its\nprincipal-value convention.\n\nFigure 6.3.3 displays |E₁(x+iy)| over -4 <= x <= 4 and -4 <= y <= 4.\nIt uses the principal value, has a cut along the negative real axis, and\nrecords logarithmic divergence of |E₁(z)| as z tends to zero.\n\nThe section notes state that the real graphs and complex surface were produced\nat NIST. The page also points to Figure 6.16.2 for the logarithmic integral.\nNo numbered mathematical displays occur in this graphics section; the formal\ndisclosures therefore record only the concrete plotting domains and the\nnegative-real-axis cut explicitly described by Figure 6.3.3.\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.3 Graphics","header":"§6.3 Graphics","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___3-Graphics/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___3-Graphics--___6___3-Graphics"}});